  "contentHtml": "<!-- Breadcrumbs -->\n      <nav class=\"breadcrumbs\" aria-label=\"Breadcrumb\">\n        <ol>\n          <li><a href=\"/\">Home</a></li>\n          <li class=\"breadcrumb-separator\"><i class=\"bi bi-chevron-right\"></i></li>\n          <li><a href=\"/blog/\">Blog</a></li>\n          <li class=\"breadcrumb-separator\"><i class=\"bi bi-chevron-right\"></i></li>\n          <li><a href=\"/blog/balancing-work-and-school/\">Balancing Work & School</a></li>\n          <li class=\"breadcrumb-separator breadcrumb-separator--last\"><i class=\"bi bi-chevron-right\"></i></li>\n          <li class=\"breadcrumb-current\" aria-current=\"page\">Sole Proprietor Hustle vs Partnering with Classmate</li>\n        </ol>\n      </nav>\n\n      <!-- Article Header -->\n      <header class=\"article-header\">\n        <div class=\"article-meta\">\n          <a href=\"/blog/balancing-work-and-school/\" class=\"article-category-badge\" style=\"background:#f3e8ff; color:#7e22ce; border-color:#e9d5ff;\">\n            <i class=\"bi bi-briefcase-fill\"></i> Balancing Work & School\n          </a>\n          <span class=\"article-meta__item\"><i class=\"bi bi-clock\"></i> 4 min read</span>\n        </div>\n\n        <h1 class=\"article-title\">Sole Proprietor Hustle vs Partnering with Classmate</h1>\n        <p class=\"article-excerpt\">How student entrepreneurs can evaluate business partnerships with friends, structure equity splits, and avoid friendship-wrecking disputes.</p>\n\n        <!-- Author Byline -->\n        <div class=\"author-byline\">\n          <div class=\"author-byline__avatar\">\n            <img src=\"/assets/images/author.webp\" alt=\"Itoya David\" width=\"48\" height=\"48\" loading=\"lazy\" onerror=\"this.src='/favicon.ico'\">\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"author-byline__info\">\n            <span class=\"author-byline__name\">Itoya David</span>\n            <span class=\"author-byline__role\">Academic Strategist & Founder</span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </header>\n\n      <!-- Smart Audio Player Widget -->\n      <div class=\"article-audio-player\" id=\"article-audio-player\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Listen to article audio version\">\n        <div class=\"audio-player__main\">\n          <button class=\"audio-player__btn-play\" id=\"audio-play-btn\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"Listen to article\">\n            <i class=\"bi bi-play-fill\" id=\"audio-play-icon\"></i>\n            <span id=\"audio-play-text\">Listen to article</span>\n          </button>\n          <div class=\"audio-player__meta\">\n            <span class=\"audio-player__duration\"><i class=\"bi bi-headphones\"></i> 4 min read listen</span>\n            <span class=\"audio-player__status\" id=\"audio-status-text\">Click to play</span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"audio-player__controls\" id=\"audio-controls\" style=\"display:none;\">\n          <div class=\"audio-player__progress-wrap\">\n            <div class=\"audio-player__progress-bar\" id=\"audio-progress-bar\" style=\"width: 0%;\"></div>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"audio-player__control-actions\">\n            <button class=\"audio-player__btn-ctrl\" id=\"audio-prev-btn\" type=\"button\" title=\"Previous paragraph\"><i class=\"bi bi-skip-backward-fill\"></i></button>\n            <button class=\"audio-player__btn-ctrl\" id=\"audio-next-btn\" type=\"button\" title=\"Next paragraph\"><i class=\"bi bi-skip-forward-fill\"></i></button>\n            <button class=\"audio-player__btn-ctrl audio-player__speed-btn\" id=\"audio-speed-btn\" type=\"button\" title=\"Change speed\">1.0x</button>\n            <button class=\"audio-player__btn-ctrl\" id=\"audio-stop-btn\" type=\"button\" title=\"Stop listening\"><i class=\"bi bi-stop-fill\"></i></button>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <!-- Article Body -->\n      <div class=\"article-body\">\n        <p>One of the most exciting moments of undergraduate life is sitting on a hostel bunk bed at 1:00 AM with a brilliant classmate, sketching out a business idea:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>*\"Bro, let's start a digital agency together!\"*</li>\n<li>*\"Let's launch a campus food delivery service!\"*</li>\n<li>*\"You know how to code, I know how to sell—we will dominate the campus and make millions!\"*</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The energy is intoxicating. You shake hands, buy a shared domain name, create a joint WhatsApp Business account, and agree to split everything <strong>50/50</strong>.</p>\n<p>Fast forward five months into the second semester:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>You are working 15 hours a week handling all customer orders, client calls, and graphic designs.</li>\n<li>Your friend is sleeping until 11:00 AM, skipping meetings, and playing video games.</li>\n<li>Yet every time profit is distributed, your partner expects an exact 50% split.</li>\n<li>Resentment boils over, shouting matches erupt in the hostel room, the business collapses, and a four-year friendship is permanently destroyed.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Every year, thousands of promising campus ventures die not from a lack of customers, but from <strong>toxic, unstructured student partnerships</strong>.</p>\n<p>Should you build your student venture as a fierce sole proprietor, or partner with a classmate?</p>\n<p>Here is the operational guide to making the right choice and structuring partnerships that survive the pressures of university life.</p>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"solo-hustle-vs-partnership-the-strategic-trade-off\">Solo Hustle vs. Partnership: The Strategic Trade-Off</h2>\n<blockquote>\n<p>* SOLO HUSTLE vs. PARTNERSHIP TRADEOFF</p>\n<p>* **SOLO PROPRIETOR:** (+) 100% of profits belong to you; zero partner arguments; instant decisions. (-) Zero coverage: If you fall sick or have exams, business stops completely.</p>\n<p>* **CO-FOUNDER PARTNERSHIP:** (+) Redundancy & scale: Partner runs the shop while you sit in the exam hall. (-) Shared profits; potential resentment if work contributions become unequal.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"the-3-non-negotiable-rules-before-partnering-with-a-classmate\">The 3 Non-Negotiable Rules Before Partnering with a Classmate</h2>\n<p>Never partner with someone simply because they are your friend, your roommate, or someone you hang out with. Partner only if they pass these three strict tests:</p>\n<h3 id=\"rule-1-the-complementary-skill-test\">Rule 1: The Complementary Skill Test</h3>\n<p>If both of you are graphic designers, you do not need a partnership—you need a freelance network.</p>\n<p>A true partnership requires <strong>complementary operational capabilities</strong>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>**Founder A (The Builder):** High technical or creative execution (writes code, bakes food, designs interfaces).</li>\n<li>**Founder B (The Seller):** High commercial execution (finds clients, manages customer DMs, handles physical deliveries, reconciles finances).</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"rule-2-the-written-1-page-operating-agreement\">Rule 2: The Written 1-Page Operating Agreement</h3>\n<p>Never rely on verbal <em>\"we are brothers\"</em> agreements. Sit down and write a simple 1-page agreement before launching:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>### 1-Page Student Partnership Blueprint</p>\n<p>></p>\n<p>* **1.** Capital Invested: Exactly how much cash each person contributed.</p>\n<p>* **2.** Defined Responsibilities: List Founder A's 3 tasks and Founder B's 3 tasks.</p>\n<p>* **3.** The Exam Coverage Schedule: Who covers operations when exams clash?</p>\n<p>* **4.** Profit Distribution: Base execution pay + quarterly profit split.</p>\n<p>* **5.** The Exit Clause: How does a partner leave if they want to focus on grades?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Both partners physically sign this document. Having written clarity eliminates 90% of future arguments.</p>\n<h3 id=\"rule-3-ditch-the-lazy-50-50-profit-split\">Rule 3: Ditch the Lazy 50/50 Profit Split</h3>\n<p>The root cause of partner bitterness is that <strong>workload is rarely 50/50</strong>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>One student takes 24 credit units with intense lab practicals.</li>\n<li>The other takes 14 credit units of light general electives.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Replace 50/50 splits with the <strong>Task Wage + Profit Pool Model</strong>:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>All business revenues flow into the joint business account.</li>\n<li>Pay the executing founder a set task fee (e.g., ₦5,000 per delivery or design).</li>\n<li>At the end of the month, whatever net profit remains is split based on equity.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>This ensures that the partner who does the heavy lifting is fairly compensated, while the other partner still earns a return on their co-ownership.</p>\n<p>If you are currently deciding how to manage your business time alongside heavy academic coursework, read our guide on <a href=\"/blog/balancing-work-and-school/time-blocking-for-working-students/\">time-blocking schedules for working undergraduates</a>.</p>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"action-checklist-partnership-decision-matrix\">Action Checklist: Partnership Decision Matrix</h2>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><span class=\"task-checkbox\"></span>Audit whether your potential partner brings complementary skills or duplicate skills.</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><span class=\"task-checkbox\"></span>Draft and sign a 1-page Operating Agreement before accepting customer money.</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><span class=\"task-checkbox\"></span>Separate personal friendships from operational business accountability.</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><span class=\"task-checkbox\"></span>Replace automatic 50/50 splits with task-based compensation plus equity dividends.</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><span class=\"task-checkbox\"></span>Establish an explicit exam-period operational handover protocol.</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><span class=\"task-checkbox\"></span>If in doubt, start as a sole proprietor and hire freelancers on task-based pay.</li>\n</ul>\n      </div>\n\n      <!-- Author Card Footer -->\n      <div class=\"author-card\">\n        <div class=\"author-card__avatar\">\n          <img src=\"/assets/images/author.webp\" alt=\"Itoya David\" width=\"72\" height=\"72\" loading=\"lazy\" onerror=\"this.src='/favicon.ico'\">\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"author-card__body\">\n          <span class=\"author-card__label\">Written by</span>\n          <h4 class=\"author-card__name\">Itoya David</h4>\n          <p class=\"author-card__bio\">Author of <em>Get Good at Hard Things</em> and founder of the Academic Comeback Package. Helping Nigerian university students master cognitive study systems, active recall, and high-performance degree execution.</p>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <!-- ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n           READER DISCUSSION, TAKEAWAYS & TOPIC REQUEST ENGINE\n           ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->\n      <section class=\"blog-community-section\" id=\"community\">\n        <div class=\"blog-community-tabs\">\n          <button type=\"button\" class=\"comm-tab active\" data-target=\"tab-comments\" onclick=\"window.switchCommunityTab('tab-comments')\">\n            <i class=\"bi bi-chat-quote-fill\"></i> Reader Takeaways &amp; Discussion (<span class=\"comment-count-badge\">0</span>)\n          </button>\n          <button type=\"button\" class=\"comm-tab\" data-target=\"tab-topics\" onclick=\"window.switchCommunityTab('tab-topics')\">\n            <i class=\"bi bi-lightbulb-fill\"></i> Request a Topic for Itoya David\n          </button>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Tab 1: Reader Comments & What I Liked -->\n        <div id=\"tab-pane-comments\" class=\"comm-tab-pane\">\n          <div class=\"comm-form-wrap\">\n            <div class=\"comm-form-header\">\n              <h3 class=\"comm-form-title\">What Did You Like Most About This Guide?</h3>\n              <p class=\"comm-form-sub\">Share your favorite takeaway, a study technique you tested, or ask a que